# Developing Gotchas (Living Doc)

Concise checklist to avoid repeating non-obvious bugs. Add new items when fixing issues.

---

## Beads (bd) Daemon & Repo ID

### Daemon won't start / ECONNREFUSED

- **"Failed to restart daemon" or "Daemon health check failed: Error: Socket error: connect ECONNREFUSED"**
  - Cause: Daemon exits on startup due to **repository ID mismatch**: the database is bound to a different repo fingerprint than the current git remote. Nothing listens on the socket, so the CLI gets ECONNREFUSED.
  - Fix: Update the database to match the current repo: run `bd migrate --update-repo-id` and confirm when prompted. If you have other clones, run the same in each so they stay in sync.
  - If you copied `.beads` from another repo or want a fresh start: `rm -rf .beads && bd init`.

